# Dispute Packet Fix - Code Changes

## Issue: Dispute Packet Not Showing After AI Diagnosis

**Problem:** After completing AI diagnosis (step 4), clicking "Continue" did not show the dispute packet (step 5).

**Root Cause:** 
1. Sidebar navigation allowed jumping to steps without validation
2. AnimatePresence mode="wait" caused rendering issues
3. Insufficient error handling for missing data

## Solution: Applied 6 Key Fixes

### File: src/App.tsx

#### Change 1: Added canAdvanceToStep Function
```typescript
// Location: After canAdvance function (~line 180-195)
// Purpose: Validates step navigation from sidebar clicks

const canAdvanceToStep = (targetStep: number) => {
  for (let step = currentStep + 1; step <= targetStep; step++) {
    if (step === 1 && !selectedIssue) return false;
    if (step === 2 && selectedTransactionIndex === null) return false;
    if (step === 3) continue; // Step 3 is always accessible
    if (step === 4 && !diagnosis) return false;
    if (step === 5 && !selectedIssue) return false;
    if (step === 6) continue; // Step 6 is always accessible
  }
  return true;
};
```

#### Change 2: Updated canAdvance Function
```typescript
// Location: ~lines 195-205
// Purpose: Stricter validation for Continue button

const canAdvance = () => {
  if (currentStep === 0) return true;
  if (currentStep === 1) return !!selectedIssue;
  if (currentStep === 2) return selectedTransactionIndex !== null;
  if (currentStep === 3) return true;
  if (currentStep === 4) return !!diagnosis && !!selectedIssue;
  if (currentStep === 5) return !!selectedIssue;
  return true;
};
```

#### Change 3: Fixed Sidebar Navigation
```typescript
// Location: Sidebar button onClick (~lines 580-590)
// Purpose: Prevent invalid step jumps

onClick={() => {
  if (step.index <= currentStep && (step.index === currentStep || canAdvanceToStep(step.index))) setCurrentStep(step.index);
}}
```

#### Change 4: Improved Diagnosis Generation
```typescript
// Location: useEffect for diagnosis (~lines 65-75)
// Purpose: More reliable diagnosis generation

useEffect(() => {
  if (currentStep === 4 && selectedIssue && !diagnosis) {
    setIsDiagnosing(true);
    const timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
      setDiagnosis(generateDiagnosisHelper(selectedIssue, evidenceCount));
      setIsDiagnosing(false);
    }, 800); // Reduced from 1600ms
    return () => window.clearTimeout(timer);
  }
  return undefined;
}, [currentStep, selectedIssue, evidenceCount, diagnosis]);
```

#### Change 5: Fixed Animation Issues
```typescript
// Location: ~line 595
// Purpose: Prevent AnimatePresence from blocking content

// BEFORE:
<AnimatePresence mode="wait">{renderStepContent()}</AnimatePresence>

// AFTER:
<AnimatePresence>{renderStepContent()}</AnimatePresence>
```

#### Change 6: Enhanced Dispute Packet Rendering
```typescript
// Location: Case 5 rendering (~lines 470-500)
// Purpose: Defensive rendering with error handling

<div className="space-y-4">
  {(() => {
    const packetData = selectedIssue && disputePackets[selectedIssue as IssueType];
    if (!packetData || packetData.length === 0) {
      return (
        <div className="rounded-3xl border border-amber-400/30 bg-amber-500/10 p-6 text-amber-100">
          <p className="font-semibold">Unable to load dispute packet</p>
          <p className="mt-2 text-sm">Please ensure you've selected an issue type and completed the AI diagnosis.</p>
          <p className="mt-2 text-xs text-amber-200">
            Issue: {selectedIssue || 'None selected'}
          </p>
          <button
            type="button"
            onClick={() => setCurrentStep(0)}
            className="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-amber-400"
          >
            Start Over
          </button>
        </div>
      );
    }
    return packetData.map((section) => (
      <div key={section.title} className="rounded-3xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-950/95 p-6">
        <h3 className="text-xl font-semibold text-white">{section.title}</h3>
        <ul className="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
          {section.details.map((detail) => (
            <li key={detail}>{detail}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ));
  })()}
</div>
```

## Testing Instructions

1. Start the app: `npm run dev`
2. Go through steps: Landing → Select Issue → Choose Transaction → Upload Evidence (optional) → AI Diagnosis
3. Click "Continue" - should now show Dispute Packet with 4-5 sections
4. Each issue type has different dispute packet content:
   - **Scam**: Incident Summary, Timeline, Containment Actions, Monitoring Guidance, Awareness Note
   - **Unauthorized**: Access Summary, Security Timeline, Immediate Actions, Evidence, Investigation Request
   - **Duplicate**: Charge Summary, Processing Timeline, Pending vs Posted, Evidence, Reconciliation Request
   - **Refund**: Refund Summary, Processing Timeline, SLA Steps, Documentation, Escalation Statement
   - **Freeze**: Freeze Summary, Timeline, Restoration Steps, KYC Documents, Restoration Request

## Deployment

After applying changes:
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Fix dispute packet not showing after AI diagnosis"
git push
```

The changes will auto-deploy to Vercel/Railway.

## Expected Result

- ✅ Dispute packet displays correctly after AI diagnosis
- ✅ Proper validation prevents invalid step navigation
- ✅ Error messages show if data is missing
- ✅ All 5 issue types have tailored dispute packet content